    {
      "id": "semantic-zoom-smoke-procedure",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Smoke Procedure",
      "position": { "x": -760, "y": -160 },
      "width": 480,
      "height": 500,
      "ports": [
        { "id": "top", "label": "top", "direction": "input", "dataType": "value", "angle": 270 },
        { "id": "right", "label": "right", "direction": "output", "dataType": "value", "angle": 0 }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Smoke Procedure",
        "markdown": "# Semantic Zoom Procedure\n\nUse browse mode on `dev.twilite.zone`. Watch the dedicated **Semantic Zoom View Specimen**: its authored surfaces literally identify themselves as ICON, SUMMARY, and DETAIL.\n\n1. Above 75%, confirm the authored DETAIL view and its boundary list.\n2. From 45% through 75%, confirm the authored SUMMARY view and short diagnostic sentence.\n3. From 20% through 45%, confirm the authored ICON view containing the `SZ` marker.\n4. From 12% through 20%, confirm the native glyph.\n5. At or below 12%, confirm the native dot.\n6. Click the specimen, then use the viewport chip; it must center that node at zoom 1.\n7. Keep the specimen focused while zooming out; it must remain readable while surrounding nodes simplify.\n8. Confirm the primitive node simplifies rather than expanding into an unavailable richer fallback.\n9. Confirm a single click selects and focuses at every level; navigation requires an explicit Open action."
      }
    },
